I've only played version 3.1.3. I spent something like 60,000 zorkmids at
the oracle, and I remember the oracle talking about things being proof
against being eroded.

Obviously, if GoP are "old leather gloves" then they need to be fireproof.
Similarly, "padded gloves" need to be rustproof. It just depends on what
they are in each particular game.

Since my time at the oracle, however, I have managed to avoid any
confusion when wishing, by specifying

    blessed erodeproof +3 gauntlets of power
            ^^^^^^^^^^

This seems to give the desired result without having to know what type
of material the gauntlets are made of beforehand.

BTW, I do remember wishing for fireproof gauntlets once, but when I
eventually identified them there was no xxxxproof. I think it was
because they were "padded gloves" in that game, and therefore they
were *already* fireproof. But not rustproof, as I found out when I
fought a rust monster.

Just my 2c worth :)

